# Line-ending policy — AUDIT_g6 §3.4, and the reason it is not the usual one.
#
# This repository was adopted byte-for-byte in commit c115757 after its entire
# post-audit state had been preserved and digest-verified (212/212, twice). The
# adoption commit is attested: `git archive c115757 | tar -x` reproduces 164/164
# tracked files byte-identically against PRESERVE_MANIFEST_g0.sha256.
#
# That attestation is only meaningful if a checkout returns exactly what was
# committed. It very nearly did not: `core.autocrlf` was `true` at system level
# on the adopting machine with no .gitattributes present, and 39+ tracked files
# carry CRLF. Staging would have rewritten every one of them, and the Step 2
# attestation would have failed on a git configuration default rather than on
# anything wrong with the project. It was caught by hand and worked around with a
# repository-local `core.autocrlf=false`.
#
# A local config setting does not travel with a clone. This file makes it travel.
#
# `-text` means: never convert, in either direction. Checkout bytes == index
# bytes == the bytes that were attested, on every platform and under any
# `core.autocrlf` value the next person happens to have set.
#
# WHY NOT `* text=auto`, the usual answer:
#   the index holds 119 CRLF files, 74 LF files and 2 genuinely mixed files.
#   Normalising would rewrite 119+ of them, changing the very bytes the
#   attestation covers and silently invalidating PRESERVE_MANIFEST_g0.sha256.
#   Mixed line endings are not tidy, but they are *what was measured*, and this
#   loop does not rewrite evidence to make it look better.
#
# tests/test_line_endings_g6.py fails if any tracked file's working-tree bytes
# stop matching its blob, which is the property this file exists to guarantee.

* -text

# Binary formats: no conversion (already implied above) and no textual diff.
*.pt      binary
*.pth     binary
*.ckpt    binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.ico     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.whl     binary
*.gz      binary
*.zip     binary
*.npy     binary
*.npz     binary
